A checkpoint 2 implementation for the C- programming language using JFlex and CUP and Java

Please note that you may need to modify the paths for CLASSPATH, JFLEX, and CUP in 
the Makefile so that the related commands can be found on your particular 
machine.  For example, the given settings in Makefile are for the Linux 
server and the commented settings are for my MacBook.

BUILD INSTRUCTIONS:

To build the parser, type "make" in the current directory, which will 
generate an executable program called "Main".

To rebuild the parser, type "make clean" and type "make" again.

TEST INSTRUCTIONS:

To test source code like "1.cm", type 

"java -cp /usr/share/java/cup.jar:. -s Main 1.cm"

and the symbol table will be outputed to 1.sym

available flags (-a: for abstract syntax tree, -s: for symbol table)